  "body": "Signed-off-by: Zach Aller <zach_aller@intuit.com>\n",
  "references": [
    {
      "commit": {
        "author": "\"Zach Aller\" <code@example.com>",
        "date": "2026-10-20T14:55:41-05:00",
        "subject": "test: build the expected short SHA the way the PR title template does (#2287)",
        "body": "makeChangeAndHydrateRepo used `git rev-parse --short=5`, which returns a\nlonger prefix when 5 characters are ambiguous among the clone's objects.\nThe shipped title template always uses `trunc 5`, so specs comparing PR\ntitles occasionally failed (e.g. \"c8efc\" vs \"c8efcf\"). Take the first 5\ncharacters of the full SHA instead.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KMbKRJK45xAEBq9tQoc9DG\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "sha": "84074e06b5adde616c1d5ea2627c07caffedcded",
        "repoUrl": "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/gitops-promoter"
      }
    }
  ]
}
